
Broadcom Mini Driver Kit (MDK)
==============================

The Broadcom MDK provides a basic programming interface and a basic
API for Broadcom network switch devices.

Package Contents
----------------

The MDK contains the following directories/components:

cdk   - Chip Development Kit
bmd   - Broadcom Mini Driver API
phy   - PHY driver Library
board - Board specific code/drivers
doc   - Documentation

Please refer to the documentation in the doc directory for a detailed
description of the MDK components and build instructions for the
sample applications.

=====================================================================

---

## Juniper SRX300 support (branch juniper-srx300-support)

Adaptations for the BCM53343 switch on the Juniper SRX300 (OCTEON III
CN7020, little-endian mips64el host):

- `examples/linux-user/linux_shbde.c`: 32-bit MMIO reads/writes are
  byte-swapped in software; the PAXB window (BAR0) maps the CMIC
  registers big-endian.
- `examples/linux-user/linux-user.c`: `shbde_iproc_paxb_init()` is
  skipped (its PAXB_ENDIANESS write persists across reset and wedges
  the device); unit base addresses widened to 64-bit (`%llx` formats)
  since the OCTEON PCIe BARs live above 4 GB.
- `cdk/shared/cdk_dev_read32.c`, `cdk/shared/cdk_dev_write32.c`: the
  BAR2 CMIC window decodes 32-bit words word-swapped and XOR-4-offset
  (logical register R at offset R ^ 4), so the dev accessors apply
  `(addr/4) ^ 1` plus a byte swap.

Build: `make -C examples/linux-user` with
`CFLAGS="-DSYS_BE_PIO=1 -DSYS_BE_PACKET=0 -DSYS_BE_OTHER=0
-DCDK_CONFIG_INCLUDE_BCM53343_A0=1"`, unit line
`--unit 0x14e4:0x8343:0x01@<BAR2-base>:<BAR0-base>` (BAR2 = linear
CMIC window first, BAR0 = PAXB second).
